    "snowbird": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Snowbird",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-11 05:45:32",
      "note": "Howdy and good morning! This is Kolton with your Snow Report for Saturday, April 11. I hope you got that sunny skiing out of your system, as we are looking at the start of some weather pattern changes today and into next week, as the storm cycle begins to roll in. Today's forecast calls for early morning snow showers with a half inch to 1\" of snow, then cloudy skies, with a high of 50 degrees and Southwest winds 10 to 16 mph. What's better than the start of new snow? Let me tell you. Snowbird is fully stacked with fun events this weekend. Test out some new skis with Dynstar Demo Day on the Plaza Deck. I'm personally rocking the M-Free 100, which feels like it was built for Snowbird. Outside Life is here hosting the Here for the Après Ski Party with a special performance by Moonlight. We've got more Plazapalooza action all weekend long, and tonight we will be celebrating with the U.S. Ski & Snowboard Hall of Fame Induction Ceremony . See what I mean? Today's event roster is full, and you won't want to miss it. Call me a conspiracy theorist, but it seems like every year right around Tax Day, we get a big April powder day. It looks like Monday and Tuesday are lining up to keep that trend rolling. The timing couldn't be more perfect for the start of The Blister Summit . Make sure you sign up so you can ski powder on the latest and greatest new gear next week. Chickadee Bowl is closed for construction as we begin upgrading Chickadee Lift into a 4-seater. If you're parking in Entry 4, your easiest mountain access will be via Who Dunnit/Creekside Road alongside the Bypass parking lot. ALL uphill travel is closed. Have fun, ski in control, keep it groovy and Give.Me.The.Bird!",
